urning radius and wider doors are required by many wheelchairs and scooters today", which names exactly the two quantities door width and turning space; a stricter reading of the lens writer''s D-2 rule (the figure''s own words) would move this figure under the owner''s open question AQ-1 (ADJUDICATION F4, 6).', '2026-11-13 22:30', 'session_2026-11-13-edmonton-checklist-pass', '2026-11-13 22:30', 'session_2026-11-13-edmonton-checklist-pass', 'claim', '>=', 0, NULL);
INSERT INTO "source_value_extractions" ("extraction_id", "ref_id", "slug", "parameter_id", "identity_code", "icf_code", "needs_code", "medical_code", "jurisdiction", "setting", "claim_type", "claimed_value", "claimed_unit", "claim_text", "source_section", "root_id", "root_type", "root_ref_id", "echo_of", "measurement_paradigm", "device_class", "root_population_note", "root_classification_basis", "contested", "file_anchor", "locator_scheme", "loc_division", "loc_part", "loc_section", "loc_subsection", "loc_paragraph", "loc_clause", "loc_subclause", "loc_division_end", "loc_part_end", "loc_section_end", "loc_subsection_end", "loc_paragraph_end", "loc_clause_end", "loc_subclause_end", "loc_note", "extraction_method", "extraction_status", "promoted_to_rdc_id", "notes", "created_at", "created_by_session", "updated_at", "updated_by_session", "figure_role", "comparator", "harm_finding", "value_as_written") VALUES (231, 'REF-01037', NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'CA', 'elevator car', 'numerical', '1500', 'mm', 'Preferred dimension of elevator car to allow for optimal turning radius of 1500x1500mm/60x60”', '5. ELEVATORS, item 5.3', NULL, 'committee_assertion', NULL, NULL, 'stated_unmeasured', 'mixed', NULL, 'The source prints this figure in its Best Practice colour (magenta; the source legend on PDF p. 1 names blue Code (required) and magenta Best Practice): the committee''s own recommendation, not attributed to a code.', 0, 'retrieval-log/session_2026-11-13-edmonton-checklist-pass/1a117aff4c5947a8.pdf', 'section', NULL, NULL, '5', '5.3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'PDF p. 5 (render p0004); colour read from the text layer (items.json)', 'full-read', 'preliminary', NULL, 'PDF p. 5, item 5.3. Source class: Best Practice, magenta. Comparator >=: a "preferred" or "recommend" figure is a floor the committee sets above the code figure (ADJUDICATION R8). The source writes "turning radius of 1500x1500mm": a square space, stored as its side (precedent: a square turning space stored as its side, extraction 211 in the first scratch database). Whether 1500 is a radius, a diameter or the side of a square is ambiguous as printed (ADJUDICATION F7). [ASSUMPTION] Lens MOB rests on the source''s PDF p. 1 sentence "a wider turning radius and wider doors are required by many wheelchairs and scooters today", which names exactly the two quantities door width and turning space; a stricter reading of the lens writer''s D-2 rule (the figure''s own words) would move this figure under the owner''s open question AQ-1 (ADJUDICATION F4, 6).', '2026-11-13 22:30', 'session_2026-11-13-edmonton-checklist-pass', '2026-11-13 22:30', 'session_2026-11-13-edmonton-checklist-pass', 'claim', '>=', 0, NULL);
INSERT INTO "source_value_extractions" ("extraction_id", "ref_id", "slug", "parameter_id", "identity_code", "icf_code", "needs_code", "medical_code", "jurisdiction", "setting", "claim_type", "claimed_value", "claimed_unit", "claim_text", "source_section", "root_id", "root_type", "root_ref_id", "echo_of", "measurement_paradigm", "device_class", "root_population_note", "root_classification_basis", "contested", "file_anchor", "locator_scheme", "loc_division", "loc_part", "loc_section", "loc_subsection", "loc_paragraph", "loc_clause", "loc_subclause", "loc_division_end", "loc_part_end", "loc_section_end", "loc_subsection_end", "loc_paragraph_end", "loc_clause_end", "loc_subclause_end", "loc_note", "extraction_method", "extraction_status", "promoted_to_rdc_id", "notes", "created_at", "created_by_session", "updated_at", "updated_by_session", "figure_role", "comparator", "harm_finding", "value_as_written") VALUES (232, 'REF-01037', NULL, 12, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'CA', 'ramp', 'numerical', '9', 'm', 'Level landings/ resting areas provided at 9m/10yd intervals along ramp', '6. RAMPS, item 6.2', NULL, 'untraced', NULL, NULL, 'stated_unmeasured', NULL, NULL, 'The source prints this figure in its Code (required) colour (blue; the source legend on PDF p. 1 names blue Code (required) and magenta Best Practice) and states on PDF p. 1 that "Alberta Building Code requires the minimum standards for accessibility": the figure restates the Alberta building code, presumed an echo (OR-19), and supplies no independent root. The code is not held here, so root_ref_id is NULL and the root is untraced (precedent: extractions 57 and 64); T-071 step 3 re-roots it when the code is admitted (lead staged with add-locator).', 0, 'retrieval-log/session_2026-11-13-edmonton-checklist-pass/1a117aff4c5947a8.pdf', 'section', NULL, NULL, '6', '6.2', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'PDF p. 6 (render p0005); colour read from the text layer (items.json)', 'full-read', 'preliminary', NULL, 'PDF p. 6, item 6.2. Source class: Code (required), blue. Comparator <=: "provided at 9m intervals" sets the longest run between landings, a ceiling on the run (ADJUDICATION F7, R8); the source does not print "maximum". Lens: the access need for effort and fatigue (A-EFFORT) on the source''s words "resting areas"; no identity is named (OD-31).', '2026-11-13 22:30', 'session_2026-11-13-edmonton-checklist-pass', '2026-11-13 22:30', 'session_2026-11-13-edmonton-checklist-pass', 'claim', '<=', 0, NULL);
INSERT INTO "source_value_extractions" ("extraction_id", "ref_id", "slug", "parameter_id", "identity_code", "icf_code", "needs_code", "medical_code", "jurisdiction", "setting", "claim_type", "claimed_value", "claimed_unit", "claim_text", "source_section", "root_id", "root_type", "root_ref_id", "echo_of", "measurement_paradigm", "device_class", "root_population_note", "root_classification_basis", "contested", "file_anchor", "locator_scheme", "loc_division", "loc_part", "loc_section", "loc_subsection", "loc_paragraph", "loc_clause", "loc_subclause", "loc_division_end", "loc_part_end", "loc_section_end", "loc_subsection_end", "loc_paragraph_end", "loc_clause_end", "loc_subclause_end", "loc_note", "extraction_method", "extraction_status", "promoted_to_rdc_id", "notes", "created_at", "created_by_session", "updated_at", "updated_by_session", "figure_role", "comparator", "harm_finding", "value_as_written") VALUES (233, 'REF-01037', NULL, 9, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'CA', 'doors (general)', 'qualitative', 'minimum-standard door widths are insufficient for many wheelchairs and scooters today; wider doors are required', NULL, 'there is a need to exceed minimum standards for accessibility where possible. For example, a wider turning radius and wider doors are required by many wheelchairs and scooters today', 'CHECKLIST FOR ACCESSIBILITY & UNIVERSAL DESIGN (introduction, PDF p. 1)', NULL, 'committee_assertion', NULL, NULL, 'stated_unmeasured', 'mixed', NULL, NULL, 0, 'retrieval-log/session_2026-11-13-edmonton-checklist-pass/1a117aff4c5947a8.pdf', 'page', NULL, NULL, '1', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'PDF p. 1 (render p0000)', 'full-read', 'preliminary', NULL, 'PDF p. 1. The source''s page-1 statement that the minimum standards are inadequate for many wheelchairs and scooters (R7 harm/inadequacy). No printed heading; the page is the document''s introduction. [ASSUMPTION] Lens MOB rests on the source''s PDF p. 1 sentence "a wider turning radius and wider doors are required by many wheelchairs and scooters today", which names exactly the two quantities door width and turning space; a stricter reading of the lens writer''s D-2 rule (the figure''s own words) would move this figure under the owner''s open question AQ-1 (ADJUDICATION F4, 6).', '2026-11-13 22:30', 'session_2026-11-13-edmonton-checklist-pass', '2026-11-13 22:30', 'session_2026-11-13-edmonton-checklist-pass', 'finding', NULL, 1, NULL);
