a wider turning radius and wider doors are required by many wheelchairs and scooters today", which names exactly the two quantities door width and turning space; a stricter reading of the lens writer''s D-2 rule (the figure''s own words) would move this figure under the owner''s open question AQ-1 (ADJUDICATION F4, 6).', '2026-11-13 22:30', 'session_2026-11-13-edmonton-checklist-pass', '2026-11-13 22:30', 'session_2026-11-13-edmonton-checklist-pass', 'finding', NULL, 1, NULL);
INSERT INTO "term_adjudications" ("adjudication_id", "observation_id", "outcome", "term_id", "rationale", "created_at", "created_by_session", "updated_at", "updated_by_session") VALUES (91, 99, 'DEFERRED', NULL, 'A design concept, not a quantity or an element. The catalogue holds TERM-017 (universal design), which is neither a parameter nor declined; not adjudicated to it here. Declining it is AQ-7.', '2026-11-13 22:28', 'session_2026-11-13-edmonton-checklist-pass', '2026-11-13 22:28', 'session_2026-11-13-edmonton-checklist-pass');
